v2.3.3 — rename the underscore pages so Jekyll cannot drop them

_page.js is the shared page shell every page except onboarding imports.
On GitHub Pages it 404s, so onboarding rendered fine and every other
page rendered nothing: Finish saved the profile, navigated, and the
dashboard module failed to load.

2.3.2 added .nojekyll, which is correct but easy to lose in a copy or a
zip. Renamed as well, so the deployment works either way:

  pages/_page.js  ->  pages/page-frame.js
  pages/_live.js  ->  pages/live-region.js

Same exports, same signatures. No API or schema change.
